  "scope": "A statement-led derivation frozen before release proves the reduced-support normal-crossing conclusion through exact conic maps, retained component multiplicities, and an analytic gradient-degree/Morse argument with explicit boundary flows. The complete printed deformation/Hessian proof was then compared. The revision supplies ambient and unit maps, the actual residue divisor, common-power level decomposition and unequal-multiplicity two-factor transports; it preserves all seven printed items and every displayed deformation/Hessian/remainder/normalization formula. The global invocation states the all-supports hypotheses of P4.7/P4.8, while each support retains its individual P4.6 conclusion. The colength-to-degree comparison is proved by the finite-module regular-sequence/Tor/Nakayama argument; it is not attributed as a supplied proof to Milnor Problem3. All actual receiving uses retain the local conclusion. No unlocated historical routine is claimed read or rerun.",
